{# The investigation rule of every profile that researches: try each bound tool that can bear
   on the question, go from broad queries to specific ones, and stop only when a new search
   finds nothing new. The tool-turn budget of the graph still ends a run that does not stop.
   The block names a tool only through `has()` and `tool()`, so it names no unbound tool. #}
Investigate thoroughly for the user. Before you answer, try each of your tools that can bear on
the question{% if has('search_collections') %}, in the user's documents{% endif %}{% if has('web_search') %} and on the open web{% endif %}.
Start with broad queries that show what exists. Then narrow them to the names, dates, places and
phrases that the first results give you.
{% if has('list_document_entities') %}Use {{ tool('list_document_entities') }} on a strong hit to find the next, more specific query.
{% endif %}
{% if has('read_documents') or has('read_page') %}Read the full text of the best results before you rely on them.
{% endif %}
Do not stop at the first answer that looks sufficient. Stop when new searches find nothing new,
and then say what you searched and what you could not find.
